version pub2025_v
  cite ssa_pub2025
  governs always
  known 2025-01-02
  note "known: the server's Last-Modified for the PDF, 2025-01-02, its earliest public stamp: earlier than the footer month's last day, 2025-01-31 ('January 2025'), the capture, 2025-02-17, and the retrieval day (§4.5). The PDF's own stamps (created and last saved 2024-11-07) don't count, since public stamps exist (D8). So the edition is known before the repeal (2025-01-05), and its figures read as SSA published them. Round 2 took the month's last day, after the repeal; round 3 the last-saved stamp. The bend points restate the Commissioner's determination for 2025 under §215(a)(1)(B) (89 FR 85276, published 2024-10-25), which the case doesn't hold; the leaflet records no date for it, so it is known at its own (§4.5, Which act; §5.3). The illustration's stipulations are in pub2025_ex_v"
